;; spec:   stdlib §5.5 S1, §7 L20 (truthiness, typed)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 8
;; audit:  clean
;; Clojure's (if (get m k) ..) and (or (get m k) default): the test of an
;; `if` accepts a bool or an Option (truthy when `some`), and `or` of an
;; Option with a default has the default's type. Today the checker takes
;; only a bool: `cannot unify (Option i64) with bool` (A11 t01, t02). The
;; Truthy library of case 007 runs the same logic over a function call.
(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((m (assoc (map-empty) 1 10)))
    (+ (if (get m 1) 1 2) (or (get m 2) 7))))
